{
  "_about": "SYNTHETIC EEG ONLY. Parameters of the simulated brain shared by app/src/sources.ts (Simulator) and scripts/synth_insight.py, so the in-app simulator and the offline generator produce the same signatures. Gains are natural-log amplitude factors (amplitude x exp(gain)) on top of the neutral resting signal. Regions per electrode: front = clamp((y - 0.2) / 0.5, 0, 1), post = clamp((-y - 0.2) / 0.5, 0, 1), side = sign(x) when |x| > 0.1 (right = +1), temporal = |x| > 0.7 and z < 0.45 (10-05 unit-sphere positions). The signatures are textbook-plausible directions, not measured effects: nothing produced from them is evidence about real brains.",
